cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NEXUS - agent governance derived from measured failures"
message: >-
  If you cite this repository, please cite the peer-facing preprint below.
  The governance and method documents are CC BY 4.0: reuse is granted, attribution is required.
  See LICENSING.md for the per-directory terms.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Martin
    given-names: Jérémy
    alias: avp9
repository-code: "https://github.com/avp9-nexus/nexus-art"
url: "https://nexus-art.org/"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and public record of NEXUS: autonomous curator agents that evaluate and
  bid on artworks on a public testnet, where every commitment of funds passes through a human
  gesture on a hardware wallet. The repository publishes the governance rules, each paired with the
  dated failure that produced it, the corrections made to claims that turned out to be false, and
  the on-chain artefacts that let a reader verify the record independently.
keywords:
  - agent governance
  - human-in-the-loop
  - agentic AI
  - LLM agents
  - hardware wallet
  - clear signing
  - blockchain
